{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vhim62dtu7lkgmehcqxv4a6zxrgttvuowtcg5ejpsjmbrdjdoaja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RaEq6ZMffNso8L5p3Xjmzh","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit C vs Rust line by line","prompt":"You are auditing a C-to-Rust translation for EXACT behavioural equivalence. Do NOT modify any file. Produce a report only.\n\nFiles (read them fully):\n- C ground truth: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-VR2NVk/c_src/src/lib.c  (958 lines, an stb_ds.h-derived dynamic array + hash map, plus `strkey` and `arr_ins`)\n- Rust translation: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-VR2NVk/translation/src/lib.rs\n\nTask: go function by function through the C file and compare against the Rust. The C file starts with ~270 lines of macro definitions — you must expand those macros mentally where the C functions use them (`stbds_header`, `stbds_arrlen`, `stbds_arrcap`, `stbds_temp`, `stbds_temp_key`, `STBDS_HASH_TO_ARR`, `STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH`, `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD`, `STBDS_ROTATE_LEFT/RIGHT`, `stbds_load_32_or_64`, `STBDS_SIPROUND`, the `arr*` macros used by `arr_ins`, etc.).\n\nCheck specifically and report ANY discrepancy, however small:\n1. Order of operations / order of side effects (e.g. `x = *p = f()` chains, assignments inside conditions, `++`/`--` placement).\n2. Integer semantics: signedness, integer promotion of `unsigned char` to `int`, sign extension when a negative `int` is assigned/cast to `size_t`, shift counts, wrap-around, `(unsigned char)` truncation.\n3. C `switch` fall-through vs the Rust equivalent (there is one in `stbds_siphash_bytes` and one non-falling-through one in `stbds_hmput_key`).\n4. `goto` / labelled-break translation (`stbds_make_hash_index` rehash loop uses `goto done`; `stbds_hmput_key` uses `goto found_empty_slot`).\n5. Loop bounds and the two-part bucket scans (`for (i = pos & MASK; i < 8; ++i)` then `for (i = 0; i < (pos