{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nthytrc7pxekonpgj7xvn5pboqrxyds76mj5dnpwoamhur7qxx6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit complete. No files were modified (my scratch dir is removed).\n\n# Audit report: `c_src/src/lib.c` vs `translation/src/lib.rs`\n\nNote: `translation/src/lib.rs` was concurrently edited during the audit (1305 → 1316 lines); all line numbers below refer to the **current** 1316-line version. The only change was the introduction of two `realloc` wrappers (see item 26).\n\n## Method\nLine-by-line macro expansion + a differential harness that `dlopen`s both `.so`s and compares return values, `stbds_array_header` (`length`/`capacity`/`temp`), every array payload byte, every `stbds_hash_index` scalar field, every bucket's `hash[8]`/`index[8]`, arena `storage`/`remaining`/`block`/`mode`, chain length, and `temp_key` (sentinel-probed, since it is uninitialised in both). Plus an `LD_PRELOAD` `malloc`/`realloc`/`free` interposer to compare allocation sequences, and coverage counters compiled into a copy of the C to prove every subtle path was actually reached.\n\n## Per-function findings\n\n| # | C lines | function | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 276–310 | `stbds_arrgrowf` (Rust 281–325) | **MATCHES.** `min_len = arrlen+addlen` (ptrdiff_t+size_t → size_t) → `wrapping_add`; `min_cap <= arrcap`; `2*arrcap` wrap; `<4` clamp; `realloc((a)?header(a):0, elemsize*min_cap+32)`; `b = b+32`; the `if (a==NULL)` init of `length`/`hash_table`/`temp`; `capacity` set unconditionally *after*. The omitted `else { STBDS_STATS(...) }` is an empty macro. `temp={0}; (void)sizeof(temp)` has no effect. |\n| 2 | 312–315 | `stbds_arrfreef` | MATCHES. |\n| 3 | 355–358 | `stbds_rand_seed` | MATCHES. |\n| 4 | 367–373 | `stbds_probe_position` | MATCHES (`hash & (slot_count-1)`, `slot_log2` unused). |\n| 5 | 375–383 | `stbds_log2` | MATCHES (incl. `slot_count==0` → 0). |\n| 6 | 360–363 | `stbds_load_32_or_64` (Rust 359–372) | **MATCHES.** Arg order `(v32, v64_hi, v64_lo)` correct; the `<<16<<16>>16>>16` no-op sequence preserved. C's `0x87b0b0fd`/`0xb504f32d` are `unsigned int` (>INT_MAX) so `v64_lo^v32` is unsigned — no sign extension; `usize` reproduces this. Constants `2147001325, 0x27bb2ee6, 0x87b0b0fd` and `715136305, 0, 0xb504f32d` correct; `seed = seed*a+b` wrapping. Verified indirectly: `idx.seed` matched across thousands of table creations. |\n| 7 | 385–472 | `stbds_make_hash_index` (Rust 374–483) | **MATCHES.** `t+1` = `t+104` (verified `sizeof(stbds_hash_index)==104`); alloc size `(slot_count>>3)*128+104+63`; `ALIGN_FWD(...,64)`; field-set order (`storage` first); all three thresholds; `<=8 ⇒ shrink_threshold=0`; assert; `ot` copy vs `memset`+seed-advance. **`goto done` → `break 'probe`** on a `loop` labelled inside the `for j`: identical control flow (continues the `j` loop). Both bucket scans (`z=pos&7..7`, then `z=0..pos&7`) and the `pos+=step; step+=8; pos&=slot_count-1` probe advance are exact. `used_count = ot->used_count` set before the rehash loop. |\n| 8 | 474–475 | `STBDS_ROTATE_LEFT/RIGHT` | MATCHES. Never called with `n==0` (13/16/17/21/32/9/31/11/22), so no `>> 64`. |\n| 9 | 477–491 | `stbds_hash_string` | **MATCHES.** `(unsigned char)*str++` → `*str_ as u8 as usize` (0..255, no sign extension); `hash = (~hash)+(hash<<18)` evaluates both operands from the old `hash`; the two `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(...)` no-ops preserved verbatim; `*21`, `+= hash<<6`, `^= ROTR(...,22)`, `+seed`. Exhaustively verified for all 1- and 2-byte strings × 5 seeds and 48 lengths × 200 random high-bit strings. |\n| 10 | 498–551 | `stbds_siphash_bytes` (Rust 547–617) | **MATCHES.** All four init words and both `^= 0x0706…/0x0f0e…` rows; SIPROUND rotations 13/32/16/17/32/21; C=2, D=4 rounds; `v2 ^= 0xff`; `v0^v1^v2^v3`. **Sign-extension quirks correct**: `d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` is an `int` that goes negative for `d[3]>=0x80` and sign-extends into `size_t` — reproduced by `load_int_le32` (`i32 → i64 → u64 → usize`). The second half `(size_t)(int_expr)<<16<<16` casts *before* shifting, so the sign bits are shifted out — Rust's `(load_int_le32(d+4)<<16)<<16` gives the same. `data = len << 56`. |\n| 11 | 532–541 | siphash tail `switch` fall-through | **MATCHES.** Rust replaces it with descending `if rem >= 7 … >= 1`, which is exactly equivalent since `len-i ∈ 0..7`. Per-case shifts correct: `case 7 ((size_t)d[6]<<24)<<24`, `6: <<20<<20`, `5: <<16<<16`, and critically **`case 4: (d[3] << 24)` has *no* `(size_t)` cast** → `int`, sign-extends. Rust: `(((*d.add(3) as i32) << 24) as i64 as u64) as usize`. Cases 3/2/1 stay positive; `case 0: break`. |\n| 12 | 553–556 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | MATCHES. |\n| 13 | 558–564 | `stbds_is_key_equal` | MATCHES (`mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` → `strcmp` of `*(char**)`; else `memcmp(key, slot, keysize)`; returns 0/1). |\n| 14 | 571–584 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | MATCHES (loop starts at `i=1`; `strreset` then free `hash_table` then free `header`). |\n| 15 | 586–629 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` | MATCHES. Both scans, `(pos & ~7)+i` (C's `~7` is `int -8` → converted to `size_t 0xFF..F8`, same as Rust `!7usize`), `return -1` on `HASH_EMPTY`, probe advance. |\n| 16 | 631–657 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | MATCHES, including the `length += 1` **before** `memset` in the NULL branch, and `*temp = -1` for the no-table case. |\n| 17 | 659–665 | `stbds_hmget_key` | MATCHES. |\n| 18 | 667–676 | `stbds_hmput_default` | MATCHES (short-circuit `a==NULL ||`, `length+=1` before `memset`). |\n| 19 | 680–710 | `stbds_hmput_key` prologue | MATCHES. Note the NULL branch here does `memset` **before** `length+=1` (opposite of `hmget_key_ts`) — Rust 827–830 has the same order. `raw_a = a; a = HASH_TO_ARR(a)`. `slot_count = table?slot_count*2:8`; `nt->string.mode = mode>=1?SH_DEFAULT:0`; `header(a)->hash_table = table = nt`. |\n| 20 | 723–764 | `stbds_hmput_key` probe loop | **MATCHES.** `goto found_empty_slot` → `break 'found_empty_slot` on a labelled `loop`; label position identical. Loop bounds `i=pos&7..8` then `i=0..pos&7` correct. Tombstone capture `(pos&~7)+i` only when `tombstone < 0` and `index[i]==-2`. **The `temp_key` asymmetry is correct**: only the *first* scan updates `stbds_temp_key(a)` (Rust 891–899); the second scan (Rust 916–929) does not. Reached 225× in coverage and verified by a sentinel-classification comparison. |\n| 21 | 765–793 | `stbds_hmput_key` insert + `switch` | **MATCHES.** `(size_t)i+1 > arrcap`; `a = arrgrowf(a,elemsize,1,0)`; the dead `raw_a = ARR_TO_HASH(a)` is mirrored (Rust 958–959, `let _ = raw_a`); `length = i+1`; `bucket->index[pos&7] = i-1`; `temp = i-1`. The `switch (table->string.mode)` is non-falling-through (every arm `break`); Rust's `match` with `const` patterns `2/3/1/_` is equivalent — `SH_NONE(0)` and any other value hit `_`/`default`. Chained `stbds_temp_key(a) = *(char**)(a+elemsize*i) = f(key)` correctly split into store-then-propagate. Verified for `string.mode ∈ {0,1,2,3,4,5,7,100,200,255}`. |\n| 22 | 796–805 | `stbds_shmode_func` | MATCHES, incl. `(unsigned char)mode` truncation (tested `mode ∈ {-2..3, 254..260}`). |\n| 23 | 807–868 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | **MATCHES.** `temp=0` set before the table-NULL check; `final_index = arrlen-1-1`; `--used_count; ++tombstone_count; temp=1`; `hash=1/index=-2`; strdup free gated on `mode==1 && string.mode==2`; the `old_index != final_index` memmove + re-find + `index[i]=old_index`; `length -= 1` **after** that block; shrink (`>>1`, gated on `slot_count > 8`) then `else if` rebuild. C's `int i = slot & 7` (declared `int`) vs Rust's `usize` is value-identical for 0..7. |\n| 24 | 870–876 | `stbds_strdup` | MATCHES. |\n| 25 | 881–918 | `stbds_stralloc` | **MATCHES.** `blocksize = 512u << (a->block>>1)` uses the *old* `block`; `++a->block` gated on the *new* `blocksize < (1u<<20)`; `sizeof(*sb)-8+len` = `8+len`; the big-block branch's quirk of splicing `sb` in as the **second** link and leaving `remaining` untouched is preserved; `p = storage->storage + remaining - len`; `remaining -= len`. `wrapping_shl` vs C's UB shift count: empirically identical (both mask to `&63` on x86-64) for `block ∈ {0..30, 128,129,130,254,255}`, including `block=255` where `++a->block` wraps to 0. Block ramp saturates at 22 in both. |\n| 26 | 920–930 | `stbds_strreset` | MATCHES (24-byte `memset`). |\n| 27 | 938–943 | `strkey` | **MATCHES.** Writes to a 256-byte file-local static (not exported in either). Byte-identical to `sprintf(\"test_%d\")` for 3,000,000 random `int`s plus every decimal boundary, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `INT_MAX`, `0`. `INT_MIN` handled via `n as i64` + `unsigned_abs()` → `\"test_-2147483648\"`. Residual bytes past the NUL after a longer previous call are also identical (neither clears the buffer). |\n| 28 | 945–958 | `arr_ins` | **MATCHES.** Hand-expansion verified: `arrpush` = `maybegrow(a,1)` (`!a \\|\\| length+1 > capacity` → `arrgrowf(a,4,1,0)`) then `a[length++] = v`; `arrins(a,i,num)` = `arraddn(a,1)` (`maybegrow` then `length += 1`) then `memmove(&a[i+1], &a[i], 4*(length-1-i))` using the **post-increment** length, then `a[i]=num`; `arrfree` = `free(header(a)); a=NULL`. Capacity sequence per iteration: `48` bytes (cap 4) → `realloc` to `64` (cap 8) → `free` — the `LD_PRELOAD` allocation traces are byte-identical (45 calls per 3 invocations). All internal asserts pass in both for `{0,1,-1,42,INT_MAX,INT_MIN,7}`. |\n| 29 | 227–247, 325–344 | struct layouts | **MATCHES** on x86-64 LP64. `stbds_array_header` 32 B (`length,capacity,hash_table,temp`), `stbds_string_block` 16 B (`next`, `storage[8]`, `storage` at offset 8), `stbds_string_arena` 24 B (`storage,remaining,block,mode`), `stbds_hash_bucket` 128 B, `stbds_hash_index` 104 B — all `#[repr(C)]` in declaration order, with compile-time size asserts. Empirically confirmed: my harness's independently-written C mirror structs read matching values from both libraries across all fields. |\n| 30 | all | constants | **MATCHE