{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_eei6dkgin4lyoicxcuoriuy7zuxijwhyc2sna5dcoprzss5df3oa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Every gate passes.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **16/16 exported, `MISSING_COUNT=0`**, no unresolved symbols either side |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | **59 rows, 0 unchecked** |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | **73 `E` + 6 `B` rows, 0 unchecked** |\n| Every feature combination | crate declares no `[features]`, so `DEFAULT` / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` is the complete set — all three pass, each against **both** the release and the debug cdylib |\n\n`./run_all.sh` → **43 OK / 0 FAIL — ALL CHECKS PASSED**. 137 tests in 8 files, all driving both `.so`s through `libloading`/`dlsym` only.\n\n## Four real divergences found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **Asserts were dead.** All 8 `STBDS_ASSERT` sites were `debug_assert!`, but `CMakeLists.txt` compiles with `C_FLAGS = -fPIC` and no `NDEBUG`, so glibc `assert` is live. Input that abnormally terminates the C was silently tolerated by Rust. → `assert!`.\n2. **Non-wrapping arithmetic.** Plain `+`/`-`/`+=` where the C wraps: fine in release, panics under `overflow-checks`. → explicit `wrapping_*`, enforced by running the whole suite against the debug cdylib.\n3. **Crash-signal mismatch.** `stbds_stralloc` used `(*p).field` on pointers the C never null-checks; Rust's debug UB check turned C's **SIGSEGV (139)** into **SIGABRT (134)**. → raw address arithmetic (`raw_load_ptr`/`raw_store_ptr`).\n4. **Allocation-call sequence.** LLVM path-split `stbds_arrgrowf`'s null branch into `malloc(n)`, but the C passes a *runtime* pointer there and really calls `realloc`. → split into `stbds_realloc` (`black_box`'d) and `stbds_realloc_fresh` (the C's literal-NULL form, which gcc folds to `malloc`). All 6 traced scenarios now match call-for-call.\n\nNotable new coverage: an `LD_PRELOAD` allocator interposer comparing 261 allocator calls; subprocess crash-parity for 5 fatal rows; self-referential keys to safely reach the mixed-mode `SH_NONE` + string-mode path; and seed engineering that forces `hash < 2` (the `hash += 2` guard) deterministically.\n\nOne newly documented C behaviour: `stbds_hmdel_key` with `mode >= 2` **and** an element swap hashes the wrong bytes and trips `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` — reproduced, not repaired (row E67).\n\nAn independent second audit with its own harness, coverage counters, and tracer reviewed all 29 functions and reported **0 divergences**. `c_src/` is byte-for-byte unmodified (md5s verified); only `c_src/build/` was added, as the task requires."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1433,"cache_read_input_tokens":423055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1433,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aae41731-ad07-4556-b28d-c5975b42818a","uuid":"b4d8fb60-7b85-4404-8971-36939d51d2e9","timestamp":"2026-08-27T06:23:44.207Z"}
